<%# A table too wide for the screen scrolls sideways inside this wrapper.

    The wrapper ships focusable and named, because a scroll container is not
    reachable with a keyboard otherwise: there is no way to see the columns
    past the right edge without a mouse or a trackpad (WCAG 2.1.1). Rendering
    it that way rather than adding it from JavaScript keeps the affordance
    when JavaScript does not run; `table_scroll_controller` then removes the
    tab stop and the landmark again on any table that fits, so only tables
    that genuinely scroll cost the reader a stop.

    Pass `labelledby:` with the id of the heading that already names the
    table, and `label:` only where no such heading exists.

    Locals: labelledby (element id) or label (string), one of the two %>
<%
  labelledby = local_assigns[:labelledby]
  label = local_assigns[:label]
  raise ArgumentError, "shared/table_scroll needs labelledby: or label:" if labelledby.blank? && label.blank?
%>
<div class="yn-table-scroll"
     data-controller="table-scroll"
     tabindex="0"
     role="region"
     data-table-scroll-role="region"
     <% if labelledby.present? %>
       aria-labelledby="<%= labelledby %>"
       data-table-scroll-aria-labelledby="<%= labelledby %>"
     <% else %>
       aria-label="<%= label %>"
       data-table-scroll-aria-label="<%= label %>"
     <% end %>>
  <%= yield %>
</div>
